{{GuideIntroClass|Temporalist}}

Range for this guide: e300-e550 [[Mysteries]].

== Introduction ==
As a brief disclaimer, this guide works MUCH BETTER with higher quality {{ItemTooltip|item_name =Temporal Stabilizer}}, {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Stabilizing Pauldrons}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Timeshroud}}. You can still make profit with lower-rarity versions of these items, but the class will be a bit weak compared to other T2s. Additionally, tempo likes longer exiles (and therefor realms) and as such can be a bit slower than other classes. It is nonetheless viable, but keep this in mind when trying to get memories.

The general gist of this guide is that you use {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}}, scaling its pet time with your skipped time, and then burst with a lot of idle bonus gear. Once you equip it in buildup, make sure to not swap to another pet afterwards.

After e550 temporalist instead uses {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Mechanos Apexis}}, which changes a lot of things about how the class is played. Due to this, there is [[Temporalist Guide (e550+)|another guide]] for {{ClassTooltip|Temporalist}} after e550 mysteries.

{{Warning|If you are planning to keep playing {{ClassTooltip|Temporalist}} and upgrading items for it, look at which ones are used in the post e550 guide since the e300-e550 range will soon be trivial for you. Additionally, focus on upgrading burst and void mana items, with the exception of the three items mentioned above.}}
===Attributes===
Your starting attributes should be :
*Intelligence : 150 (130 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Circlet Of Deep Thoughts}})
*Insight : 150 (65 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Netherfist}})
*Spellcraft : 175
*Wisdom : 0
*Dominance : 0
*Patience : 200 (or whatever your max is, this is your highest priority)
*Mastery : 75
*Empathy : 35
This may be a bit off from what you can actually do at e300, but this should be your goal.<br>
Keep in mind that it is most important to have the attributes to equip whatever burst and void mana items you will be using. The above assumes using the items in the guide, but you may want to change these since you don't have them all at legendary.<br>
From here, you always want to keep Patience maxed to whatever your attribute cap is. After that, go for Spc200, and then Int200 (keep in mind that  {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Circlet Of Deep Thoughts}} gives you 20 Int for free), and then either Ins140 (160 without maxed {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Netherfist}}), or potentially Mas100+. Mas100 might be worth it if you can't get a full 50 points for Spc200/Int200, although I'm not quite sure. Int225/250 are very strong when you unlock them, as are Spc225/250 - go for whichever one gives you the highest number between Int250 and Spc250.

== Overview ==
Temporalist has a few major sources of scaling - skipped time from {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole}} (which affects its class ability, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Superposition}} and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}}), {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Ley Overdrive}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=True Sorcery}}, and most importantly {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Quasi-incantation}}. We attempt to stack as much of these as possible, in varying amounts. 

The spell {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Void Radiance}} is our choice for generating void mana, because we can't switch off of {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}} without losing its scaling.

We then [[Snap]] the spell {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Stabilize The Flow}} and burst with as much idle bonus gear as possible. This is because {{PetTooltip|Risen Giant|RG}} gives us an additional scaling of idle^1.01 (meaning idle^2.01 overall, without items).

=== Phase Scalings ===
Here are the scalings of each phase in order for you to choose appropriate items if yours aren't all legendary yet. Unique items are especially strong early on, since they're already enchantable, meaning things like  {{ItemTooltip|Head Of The All-Eater}} are worth a look.<br>
Startup:<br>
This phase uses similar items to buildup.<br>
Scry:<br>
Things which increase the amount of accumulated and persistent casts are useful.<br>
Buildup:<br>
{{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}} scales off of log(evo), and Character level ^1. This means that you should equip evocation efficiency (and CAP due to temporalist's ability) and character experience if you can. As mentioned before, the most important pieces are {{ItemTooltip|Temporal Stabilizer}}, {{ItemTooltip|Timeshroud}} and {{ItemTooltip|Stabilizing Pauldrons}}. If you are struggling with shards, consider items which contribute to them.<br>
VM scaling:<br>
* VpE ^1
* Incant ^1.2

Snap scaling: 
* Incant ^1
* Time Distortion ^2 (we always wear {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Timeshroud}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Stabilizing Pauldrons}} because of this)

Burst scaling:
* Evo/CAP/VProfit/Profit ^1
* Idle ^2.01
* Incant ^4
* PAP ^0.6
