== The Run ==
===Startup===
'''Goals:'''
* Get enough character EXP to unlock {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole}}
* Stack up autoclicks and void entities with {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Pixie}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Synthetic Entity}}, respectively, because character EXP translates to profits for tempo
* Max available mana sources

Start by using {{ClassTooltip|Chronomancer}} with {{PetTooltip|Simulacrum}} and {{SpellTooltip|Wormhole}} to maximize your sources, as these increase your character experience. Alternatively you can do this on temporalist if you can already cast refined wormhole.

We start with {{PetTooltip|Ley Keeper}} in order to use {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}} before we actually have the experience for it. The exact level you need without it should be in the range of 190-200. Once you are a bit higher on mysteries and have some {{SpellTooltip|True Sorcery}} stacks, you have enough experience to immediately use {{PetTooltip|Pixie}} instead.
{{GuideBox
|pet1=Ley Keeper
|pet=Pixie|
spells=#0#CharXP@65,2;71,2;61,2;29,2;110,2;67,1|
items=#0#CharXP@106;104;0;23;14;35;41;60;58;85;70;1008;210;300;410;405;90;2007;3007;504}}

While necessary, this phase contributes relatively little to your overall profits, so assuming you can already cast {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}} without {{PetTooltip|Ley Keeper}} you shouldn't spend much more than 10 minutes here.

===Scry===
Goals:<br>
*Stack {{SpellTooltip|True Sorcery}}, {{SpellTooltip|Ley Overdrive}} and {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}}
Here we Scry a few accumulated spells. Spend around 10% of your exile here.<br>
In case you're struggling to use {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}} even after startup, sit on this set to stack {{SpellTooltip|True Sorcery}} until you can. This might take quiet a while, but you only need to do this once per realm and the additional experience also contributes to profit.
{{GuideBox|pet=Arcanaworg|
spells=#1#Scry@21,2;57,2;61,2;65,2;0,2;67,2|
itemtab=Items|items=#1#Scry@113;101;2;24;12;39;41;68;56;88;72;1023;209;304;415;405;97;2003;3008;509|
}}

===Buildup===
'''Goals:'''
*Stack {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Quasi-incantation}}
*Skip time with {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole|display_name=Wormhole}}

Buildup is a bit awkward on {{ClassTooltip|Temporalist}}, since you need three of your spellslots to skip time and one to cast {{SpellTooltip|Quasi-incantation}}. As these are our most powerful tools, we want to have them on the bar as much as possible. This leaves us with two slots to do as we want. And what we want is to use {{SpellTooltip|True Sorcery}} and {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}} to make timeskip and quasi-incantation stronger. Spend about 90% of your exile here.
{{GuideBox|pet=Risen Giant|
spells=#2#Buildup@65,2;21,2;61,2;93,2;110,2;67,1|
itemtab=Items|items=#2#Buildup@113;101;0;23;14;35;41;60;58;85;77;1008;209;304;415;405;90;2007;3007;504|
note= 
* These items should be your lowest priority to upgrade, by far. They should be upgraded, but ''only'' after burst, vm, and snap are all done first, and by that point you'll likely be out of this range, and should be focusing on the e550+ version of this guide. <br> * You'll notice we use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Greater Elemental}} - this is to help cast {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Quasi-incantation|display_name=QI}} before unlocking {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Scabbard}}. See the section about Cast Ratios below. <br> * If you don't have {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Ritual Disk}}, you can use {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Zenith, The Champion's Steed|display_name=Zenith}} (with PP) or {{ItemTooltip|item_name=The Rubedo Engine|display_name=Rubedo}} (with LO). Disk is far better, though - prioritize completing the Brain Fog triumph if you plan to play Temporalist in the future. <br> * {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Stabilizing Pauldrons}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Timeshroud}}, are '''especially important to upgrade''', because they increase max Time Distortion, which directly increases your time skipped, and also massively increases profits from {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Stabilize The Flow}}. Prioritize them over any other gear in this set.{{ItemTooltip|item_name =Temporal Stabilizer}} is also equally, if not more, important.}}

'''Note:''' Before spending too much time on buildup, do a quick burst in order to get more upgrades and character experience.

You'll want to stay in buildup for as long as you need to gain enough profit to be satisfactory to you. Temporalist is a relatively slow class, meaning your exiles start off relatively weak. On the flipside, on longer exiles it will give more profit than most other classes.

=== Pet XP Phase ===
'''Goals:'''

* Gain as much Pet XP as possible. Do not linger here for too long.
{{GuideBox|pet=Risen Giant|spells=#9#PetXP@65,2;67,1;26,2;21,2;25,2;110,2|items=#9#PetXP@115;106;9;27;13;31;41;66;57;85;70;1008;203;300;406;415;96;2009;3007;506}}

===Void Mana ===
'''Goals:'''

* Get as much VM as possible.

We use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Void Radiance}} because Risen Giant's profit bonus is scaled based on our time spent using it (including skipped time), so {{PetTooltip|Voidterror}} is out of the question. Here are our sets:

{{GuideBox|pet=Risen Giant|
spells=#3#VM@30,2;34,2;65,1;67,1;3,0;61,0|
itemtab=Items|items=#3#VM@113;111;5;25;15;30;49;68;55;89;78;1005;202;309;412;407;99;2010;3006;503|
note=* Using {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Insidious Lure}} is better than {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Anima Core}}, although it's not likely you have it at this point. <br>
* If you don't have {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Crystallized Echo}}, you can use {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Ritual Disk}}. Nothing else will help here. <br>
* We use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Kelphior's Black Beam|display_name=KBB}} to charge up {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Reality Prism}} here, and because nothing else matters. If you aren't using Reality Prism, you can use {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Head Of The All-Eater}} and charge it up, although you should use {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Stabilizer}} for the actual gaining of VM in that case - both it and Reality Prism are used mostly for the incantation efficiency enchantment here. Thus, we usually use Reality Prism since it is also enchanted for burst. }}

Don't stay on this phase for very long, no more than 1-5 minutes.

===Snap===
Here, we snap {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Stabilize The Flow}}, because it will keep the profit bonus it had when cast for its entire duration. This means getting time distortion as high as possible and maximizing our incantation efficiency on our gear, manually casting StF, and then swapping to burst. Here are our sets for this:

{{GuideBox|pet=Risen Giant|
spells=#4#Snap@73,2;65,2;61,2;67,1;69,0;3,0|
itemtab=Items|items=#4#Snap@113;104;7;23;18;32;41;68;56;85;72;1005;209;301;411;409;91;2007;3001;509|
note= * If not using Reality Prism in burst, then use Temporal Stabilizer for this phase, as we only care about the incantation efficiency. <br>
* There aren't really any other substitutions to make; you just need to maximize incantation efficiency. This set is your lowest priority besides buildup, but it is still important.}}

These spell sets are the pre-burst setup, though this specific type of setup is also known as a [[Snap|"Snap"]]. Here's how it goes in this case: 
<br>
Swap to this set (via Q+5). Then, after reaching your maximum time distortion, either swap your spellset to burst via Z/Y+6 or manually cast StF. Finally, swap fully to burst with Q+6.

===Burst===
'''Goals:'''

* Maximize profit!!

Here's our burst sets. 

{{GuideBox|pet=Risen Giant|
spells=#5#Burst@73,2;57,2;61,2;17,2;69,2;3,2|
itemtab=Items|items=#5#Burst@113;104;1;20;14;33;47;68;54;83;76;1005;207;306;411;404;94;2005;3004;507 |
note=* Although upgrading Reality Prism should be a priority, you can use {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Head Of The All-Eater}} instead. If doing that, replace KBB with {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Singularity Beam}}.
* You can burst using a gear set that looks more like the e550+ guide, if you don't want to spend the dust on idle bonus gear, but these will be far better due to RG's bonus based on idle bonus, making it roughly ^2.02 to profit. This is also why we maximize PAT.
* There are probably some differences at 0/low enchants, but I can't be bothered! It's good enough.}}

You don't want to burst more than the duration of StF, although you ''can'' use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Revert}} to refresh it and keep bursting for a bit. Always reburst (meaning do vm -> snap -> burst again) at least once per exile, because you'll likely get upgrades that give you incantation efficiency or VpE.